course: dictionary
lesson: 8326
title: Rodeo: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so you need the context to know which one is right. Cousin Jake from Texas came to stay and said he'd ridden a real bull at a rodeo «for like ten minutes». The words bull, Texas and ridden tell you a rodeo here is a show with animals and riding, not a dance or a party.
explain: A rodeo is a show and competition where cowboys and cowgirls ride bucking horses and bulls, rope calves and race horses round barrels. Rodeos happen in ranching areas, such as parts of the USA, Canada, Australia and Mexico. Canada's Calgary Stampede is one of the most famous.
explain: Informal meanings are different. If someone says «This isn't my first rodeo», they are not talking about horses at all: they mean «I have done this before, so I have experience». In an informal way, a rodeo can also mean any noisy, chaotic event, like a messy party. Ask yourself: does the sentence mention animals, riding or ropes? If not, look for a different meaning.
fact: A rodeo is a show and competition with riding and roping events.
fact: Rodeo events include riding bucking horses and bulls, roping calves, and racing horses round barrels.
fact: «This isn't my first rodeo» means «I have done this before, I have experience».
fact: Rodeos are found mainly in ranching areas of the USA, Canada, Australia and Mexico.
fact: Some people think rodeos are cruel to animals, while others say they are a tradition; both views are discussed.
exercise: «Cousin Jake from Texas came to stay and said he'd ridden a real bull at a rodeo for like ten minutes.» Where did Jake ride the bull? | In a shop | *At a rodeo show | At school | In a swimming pool
exercise: Mum says, «This isn't my first rodeo.» What does she mean? | She is at a horse show for the first time | *She has done this kind of thing before and knows what to do | She has never seen a cowboy | The party is noisy and chaotic
exercise: Which country is home to the famous Calgary Stampede, a big rodeo? | Mexico | Australia | Scotland | *Canada
test: «The school disco was a total rodeo, with everyone shouting and running into each other.» What does rodeo mean here? | *A noisy, chaotic event | A show of ropes and horses | A cowboy race | A quiet reading time
test: Some people say rodeos are cruel to animals, and others say they are a tradition. What does this show? | *Both views are discussed, so people disagree about rodeos | Rodeos are banned everywhere in the world | Everyone agrees rodeos are fine | Rodeos are only for cats
exam: Which activity happens at a rodeo? | Baking bread | Swimming in the sea | *Roping calves | Reading poems in a library
